    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Was wondering if it's possible to implement this using `mini.comment` or even with the now built-in comment mapping. I'm unfortunately not familiar enough with vimscript to figure out how to cleanly do this.\r\n\r\nI've implemented this in [cherryman/vim-commentary-yank](https://github.com/cherryman/vim-commentary-yank/), but looking for a neovim specific solution.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Was wondering if it's possible to implement this using <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.comment</code> or even with the now built-in comment mapping. I'm unfortunately not familiar enough with vimscript to figure out how to cleanly do this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've implemented this in <a href=\"https://github.com/cherryman/vim-commentary-yank/\">cherryman/vim-commentary-yank</a>, but looking for a neovim specific solution.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Was wondering if it's possible to implement this using mini.comment or even with the now built-in comment mapping. I'm unfortunately not familiar enough with vimscript to figure out how to cleanly do this.\nI've implemented this in cherryman/vim-commentary-yank, but looking for a neovim specific solution.",
